  "text": "Copy/\nExpression by fan if Indon Mride f\n- Customa\nT.&C. \"09/3311\nTariff Administration - Exemption Machine Tools,\nTools of Trade, and Minor Articles.\nTariff Item 166.\nMachine Tools as prescribed by Departmental\nBy-laws\nFree.\nTariff Item 168.\nTools of Trade for the use of artisans and\nmechanics and\ntools in general use\nas prescribed by Departmental\nBy -laws\nFree.\nTariff Item 434.\nMinor articles prescribed by Departmental\nBy-laws for use in\nthe manufacture of goods within the Commonwealth\nThe powers exercised by the Minister under the above\nauthorities seem to me to be of special importance\nand I think it\ndesirable to place on record my opinion as to the proper course to be\nobserved in carrying out the intention of Parliament.\nThe Ministerial power in the above\nregard is purely\ndiscretionary and in every\ncase must be supported by\nsubstantial\nreasons for favorable consideration.\nThe mere fact that Machine Tools, Minor Articles, or Tools\nof Trade, are not,\nand are not likely to be\nmanufactured in\nAustralia,\nis in itself no sufficient reason for exemption.\nOn the other hand the fact that any of these articles are\ncormercially manufactured in Australia must, unless under\nthe most\nexceptional circumstances, debar their inclusion in the Exempt list.\n1imn must. necessarily be\nmay only\n-2-\nintrease the number of factories, I then consider that an application\nfor exemption should receive serious and perhaps favorable consideratio\nMior Articles.\nA similar course should be observed with\nthese,\nas ndicated above in regard to Machine Tools.\nWhst at time of exemption the articles in question may not\nbe commerally manufactured in the Commonwealth care must be taken\nto exercisa periodical revision to remove them from\nthe list as\nsoon as its ascertained\nthat they are so manufactured unless very\nspecial reons such as outlined above may be adduced in justification\nof their rention.\nBut if it is proposed to estauriou a \"-\nCommonwealth or it is shown an industry already established has vuu\nlittle Tariff assistance, or if the exemption would tend largely to",
